B. Major issues
B1. f(a,b) collapses to a single comma argument (c.y:147, expression.rs:76).
expression '(' expression ')' takes one Option<ExpressionNode>; f(a,b,c) becomes FunctionCall(f, Some(List(a, List(b,c)))). The distinction between f(a,b) and f((a,b)) is recoverable only by comparing the argument span against the call-paren span (paren rule discards the wrapper at c.y:141). Any future type-checking/codegen of calls must split top-level Expression::List nodes with fragile span heuristics. Better: Vec<ExpressionNode> args. Nothing in the current analyzer consumes expressions yet, so it's latent.
B2. Variadic function definitions panic (resolution.rs:272).
int f(int a, ...) { … } is valid C90; it reaches FunctionParameters::Variadic(_) in visit_function_definition → unimplemented!() → panic.
B3. Error recovery is cosmetic; parser exits 0 on syntax error.
The grammar defines no error production, so unwind() (yacc.rs:1044) pops the whole stack and yyabort()s. All yyerrok/token_since_error/is_recovering machinery (yacc.rs:1093-1107) is dead code — only one error is ever reported. Worse, main.rs:27 ignores the parse outcome, so a file with a syntax error still exits 0 (and AstPrinter is commented out).
B4. goto target label is dropped (c.y:435).
JumpStatement::Goto stores no Name; the label is never resolvable. case/default also have no switch-context validation and continue/break no loop-context check (all semantic).
B5. Anonymous struct/enum with body but no tag: ENUM '{' … '}' creates a new distinct tag every occurrence (c.y:370). In C90 an anonymous-enum-in-declaration is expected (each is a distinct type), so this is arguably OK; but struct { … } anonymous with ctx.struct_or_union(tag, None, …) (context.rs:41) also always allocates a fresh struct — fine for C90 semantics. Low severity, listed for completeness.
C. Minor / hygiene
- C1. yyerror uses lexer.span, not the offending token's span; combined with the parser using self.lexer.span at shift time, diagnostics can point one token late in some conflicts.
- C2. 08/09 lexed as valid constants (c.l:56): 0{D}+ matches 08, no octal-digit validation → invalid octal accepted silently (gcc errors under -pedantic-errors). Integer suffixes (ll, mixed uU) also never validated.
- C3. // comments (c.l:20), trigraph ??/ (missing), stray ??= (not #), catch-all . bad-char skip (c.l:110) are all silently tolerated extensions/leniencies rather than pedantic errors.
- C4. $ etc. silently dropped (., c.l:110) can mangle identifiers without any warning.
- C5. AST/parser coupling: Expression::unary/binary/access dispatch on raw YYToken variants (expression.rs:144-204), so the AST module imports parser tokens; any operator addition requires touching grammar + generated yacc.rs + expression.rs. A dedicated operator enum would decouple.
- C6. Debug leftover println!("COUCOU") in resolution.rs:122.
- C7. is_tentative_definition is inverted (external.rs:140): returns true only when there is an initializer; a tentative definition is one without one. (Semantic, not parser, but adjacent.)
- C8. %left ',' ordering vs the rest (c.y:47-48) is correct (PREC_NO_COMMA binds tighter than comma, correctly stopping case 1,2: / int a = 1, b = 2).
- C9. Declarations-after-statements rejected syntactically (grammar splits declaration_list/statement_list, c.y:402-404) rather than as a constraint diagnosis — output differs from gcc wording, which the project flags as acceptable, but the error class differs.
